ns[col - s];\\n            if (window > maximum) maximum = window;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    std::printf(\\\"%lld\\\\n\\\", maximum);\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Replacing repeated strided edge reductions with O(N^2) rolling column sums exposes contiguous, independent 64-bit updates suitable for legal ARM64 SIMD.\",\n  \"notes\": \"Not executed or measured. Retains the existing cin/scanf input path and single-threaded execution. The dependent horizontal rolling scan is deliberately not marked independent.\",\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Flatten the full matrix into contiguous row-major storage without changing input parsing.\",\n    \"Maintain each column's S-row sum using independent unit-stride initialization and entering-minus-outgoing updates.\",\n    \"Compute each row of candidate windows with a scalar horizontal rolling scan.\",\n    \"Use 64-bit intermediate arithmetic, casting before subtraction, and apply GCC ivdep only to dependency-free column loops.\"\n  ]\n}"}}
